  "summary": "I wrote src/main.ts and it passes typecheck. I did not run `vite build` or load it in a browser, so none of it has been checked visually. It builds a 260×260 ground plane and 10,000 instanced objects: 8,000 trunks (cylinders) and 8,000 canopies (cones), plus 2,000 rocks (spheres). Placement uses a fixed-seed LCG, so the forest is the same on every load. Canopies and rocks get per-instance HSL colours from a white base material. The scene has one shadow-casting directional light, a hemisphere fill light, and exponential fog (`effects.fog` with `mode: \"exp\"`, density 0.0045). The orbit camera auto-rotates at 0.12 rad/s with the whole forest in view. The engine's `createAuraApp` runs the render loop. After `await app.ready()` I set `window.__EVAL_READY__ = true` inside a `requestAnimationFrame` callback. I wrote no `requestAnimationFrame` loop myself, so the \"render continuously\" part of the contract relies on the engine's loop.",
